recap: 'Separate factual content, creative direction and publication checks. Make the result usable to people who cannot see or hear the media.', sources: [NIST, 'https://www.w3.org/WAI/tutorials/images/', 'https://www.w3.org/WAI/tutorials/images/complex/'],
checks: [['Which is the best tool choice for an exact subnet diagram?', ['An unchecked generated photograph', 'A structured diagram with verified labels', 'A random stock image'], 1, 'Exact relationships and text are better expressed with controlled diagram tools.'], ['A chart uses fictional performance data. How should it be presented?', ['As proof of customer results', 'Without any labels', 'Clearly labelled illustrative data with units and a table'], 2, 'Readers must be able to distinguish teaching examples from measured evidence.']]
